// expect: 40
// The theorem the emit's floor-twin arithmetic stands on: a wide
// instantiation reaches its OWN twin even through a REFERENCE (the generic
// `add` passed to a Float fold), so a quantified var still free at emit is
// a floor word. 1.5 + 2.5 == 4.0 through the reference — measured 40 on
// boots 5bf55b68 and 1ff80ffb before the numeric gate landed, and held.
fn add(a, b) = a + b

fn main() = if fold(0.0, add, [1.5, 2.5]) == 4.0 { 40 } else { 41 }
